                                                "sense_id": "93f5a23b-a253-3d49-a03b-57407518c4a2",
                                                "text": "To use a strong decoction of the vegetable bitters as a substitute for alcohol—such, for example as wormwood, chamomile, horehound, southernwood and tanzy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8b38464-a8e2-4ffc-9093-d9b1196b7b73",
                                                "sense_id": "93f5a23b-a253-3d49-a03b-57407518c4a2",
                                                "text": "According to the Roman Pliny the Elder, author of Historia Naturalis, southernwood was conducive to sexual excitement when the plant was placed under the bed."
                                            }
